Characteristics of Java 8 Streams
3.1) Streams are not the data structures
  Streams doesn't stores the data. We can't add or remove elements from stream
  Hence, they are not data structures. They are the just operations.

3.2) Stream consumes a data source
  Stream consumes a sources, perform operations on it and produces the result,
  Source may be collection or array or an IO resource, but remember, stream doesn't modify the source.
  They don't have their own source of data.

3.3) Intermediate and terminal Operations
   Most of the stream operations return another new stream and they can be chained together to form a pipeline of operations.
   The operations which return stream themselves are called Intermediate Operations. e.g. filter(),distinct(),sorted().
   The operations which return other than stream are called Terminal Operations. e.g. count(),min(),max().